  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 301 AM CDT Wed Jul 1 2026\n\nWednesday through next Tuesday: \n\nHigh pressure continues to encompass the southeast CONUS, providing \nongoing dangerous heat over the region. Persistent highs ranging in \nthe mid-upper 90s, combined with mid 70 dewpoints will result in \nheat indices between 110-115 degrees in the MS Delta/portions of \ncentral MS areas and heat indices up to 110 degrees outside of those \nareas. An Extreme Heat Warning will go in effect at 10AM in areas\nwith heat indices 110+ and a Heat Advisory will remain in effect \nelsewhere. Heat precautions should be considered, especially with \nlong-term outdoor exposure. A weak disturbance will progress over \nthe area, providing isolated shower/storm chances through the \nevening. With an unstable airmass present, a marginal (1 out of 5)\nrisk for severe weather will be possible during the afternoon and\nevening hours. \n\nHigh pressure will gradually slide northeastward Thursday, keeping \nafternoon rain chances and dangerous heat over the area. Extensions \nof the heat products will be evaluated on a day to day basis. Hot \nconditions will continue into the 4th of July weekend. A couple of \ndisturbances may provide diurnal showers and storms over the holiday \nand Sunday. Dangerous heat along with rain chances will persist into \nnext week. /SW/",
